# Where fw_printenv / fw_setenv find the U-Boot environment.
#
# Format is one line per copy: <device> <offset> <size>.
#
# THIS MUST ADDRESS THE SAME BYTES AS CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET, and it reaches them a
# different way, which is the thing to understand before editing either:
#
#   U-Boot's env_blk.c ignores the partition table entirely and writes at the raw
#   byte offset CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET = 0x3F8000 (sector 8128) on the boot device.
#   fw_setenv here opens the uboot_env *partition* and writes at offset 0 within it.
#
# Those are the same 32 KiB only because the wks places uboot_env at exactly
# sector 8128 with size 32 KiB = 0x8000. Three files have to agree:
# meta-microduck/files/wic/microduck-ab.wks.in (the partition),
# recipes-bsp/u-boot/files/rauc-env.cfg (CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET), and this one.
# Change one and RAUC writes an environment U-Boot never reads -- with no error
# from either side, because each is doing exactly what it was told.
# scripts/check-wks-layout.py cross-checks all three.
#
# by-partlabel, never a partition number: numbers have shifted twice in this
# layout already, most recently when v_storage was added ahead of uboot_env.
#
# One line, so a single copy, no redundancy -- see rauc-env.cfg for why
# CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND is deliberately absent on this backend. A torn write
# loses the environment and U-Boot falls back to its compiled-in default.
/dev/disk/by-partlabel/uboot_env 0x0000 0x8000
